{"result":"{
  "id": "19433",
  "key": "SFCC-867",
  "summary": "Cart – Screen Reader Announcement Rules for Error & Warning Messages",
  "description": "As a Shopper using a screen reader, I want error and warning messages in the cart to be announced in a clear and prioritised order, so that I am informed of the most important issue without being overwhelmed by multiple simultaneous announcements.\n\nWhen a cart error condition exists, up to three error messages can display simultaneously: a page-level banner (SFCC-404), an inline item error on the affected line item (SFCC-795), and an error message in the order summary (SFCC-274). \n\nA screen reader will not automatically read all three — the PWA Kit codebase must define explicit rules to determine which message is announced, in what order, and when.\n\nThis story covers the screen reader announcement rules and priority order for all cart error and warning states. It does not cover the visual display of error messages — each component story owns its own visual treatment.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  }
}"}

